(text "TS06-DRV  ·  185 V converter"
(exclude_from_sim no)
(at 20.32 12.7 0)
(effects
(font
(size 3 3)
(bold yes)
)
(justify left top)
)
(uuid "7aae98c5-5cde-571d-8842-f5a70fe579eb")
)
(text "L1, the IRF840 and a fast 600 V rectifier boost 12 V to the 185 V anode rail, HV185, held in a 4.7 uF 400 V reservoir whose bleeder makes it safe\nabout 10 s after power-off. D9's clock reaches the MOSFET through a TC4420 driver, and an LM393 holds the driver's input low while the divided rail is\nabove a 2.5 V reference. The 5k trimmer sets 165-210 V; its wiper is on the grounded end, so an open wiper lowers the rail."
(exclude_from_sim no)
(at 20.32 19.05 0)
(effects
(font
(size 1.524 1.524)
)
(justify left top)
)
(uuid "f8860107-0500-505b-8bcd-50b62e9c0804")
)
(text "Notes from tools/ts06pair.py"
(exclude_from_sim no)
(at 20.32 146.05 0)
(effects
(font
(size 1.524 1.524)
(bold yes)
)
(justify left top)
)
(uuid "6afcf893-ce5d-53b6-ba85-6d282d0b500e")
)
(text "C7: The reservoir, 400 V.\nL1: 220 uH, Isat >= 1.8 A (1.3 A peaks at 12 V in, 23.8 us on).\nR60: Bleeder: the reservoir is safe ~10 s after power-off.\nR62: Divider top, two in series, each under 100 V.\nR65: Hysteresis, about 1 V of rail.\nR69: 2.5 V reference.\nRP1: Rail set-point 165-210 V; wiper on the grounded end, so an open wiper lowers the rail.\nU11: Non-inverting MOSFET driver, 12 V out. MCP1407 is a drop-in.\nU12: Comparator: FB above VREF holds the driver input low. Second half parked.\nVD1: Fast 600 V rectifier: 1 cathode, 2 anode.\nVT21: 500 V switch, G-D-S, standing. Pads narrowed for 0.94 mm drain clearance."
(exclude_from_sim no)
(at 20.32 148.59 0)
(effects
(font
(size 1.27 1.27)
)
(justify left top)
)
(uuid "6f8aff2d-c0c1-5467-b904-8e166894f303")
)
